<!--
  Principles that recur across agent-tooling repos and are worth considering for yours.
  Delete the ones that do not apply rather than keeping them as filler.

  - REFUSAL IS A RESULT, NOT AN EXCEPTION. Return {error, message, guidance}; the
    guidance names the cheapest correction rather than restating the rule. A caller --
    especially an agent -- reports a raised refusal as a failure of the whole task.

  - CHOOSE THE REFUSAL CHANNEL BY REMEDY, NOT BY SEVERITY. Two failures that need
    different fixes are different channels even when they are equally bad. If a remedy
    is "change local configuration", it cannot share a channel with "pass a different
    argument", because no other channel can ask for the first.

  - ABSENCE IS NEVER REPORTED AS CLEANLINESS. An empty finding list can mean the check
    ran and found nothing, or that the column was missing and it never ran. Publish
    which, every time -- `checks_run`, `columns_unavailable`, `checks_skipped`.

  - EVERY THRESHOLD NAMES WHOSE IT IS. FIELD CONVENTION / MODELLING ASSUMPTION /
    MEASURED <date> / NOT ESTABLISHED. An unlabelled number is a defect, and
    NOT ESTABLISHED is an honest label rather than a gap.

  - THE TOOL DOES NOT JUDGE; THE HUMAN DOES. Return located signals with what each
    one shows and does not show. A signal relayed as a defect is a judgement the tool
    was not entitled to make.

  - EVERY RESULT CARRIES DIAGNOSTICS. Freshness, source, caveats -- attached to the
    payload, not left in a docstring where the caller will not see them.

  - COUNT BEFORE YOU FILTER. A count taken after a limit or a filter is a different
    number from the one its name implies, and it will be quoted as a total.

  - THE SERVER COMPOSES EVERY QUERY. Caller-supplied strings select from a whitelist;
    they never reach a query, a path or a URL shape.

  - FAIL FAST UPSTREAM, DEGRADE LATERALLY. Direction, not severity: a bad input stops
    the pipeline, a missing optional signal continues with the absence recorded.
-->

